LAURA LOOMER: When I was in Israel, I met with high-ranking military officials and politicians and discussed embracing the end of US aid to Israel. The United States benefits more from Israel than they do from us anyway.

If we do away with aid to Israel, then we wouldn't even need AIPAC at all, so the whole Israeli interference in our elections narrative would disappear. America First means not telling other countries what to do.

@LauraLoomer

NEW: We just spoke exclusively with Congresswoman Haley Stevens at a polling place in Birmingham Michigan as she came to cast her ballot for Republican Mike Rogers. She told us she’s here to vote with her mother and that she still believes Democrats will win the majority, “It's the people's day. And I told this to our next speaker of the house, Hakeem Jeffries: It's Majority Makers Day.”

I asked if given the backlash she’s receiving from her Rogers endorsement, whether she feels it was worth it and she told me “Absolutely. Voting is always worth it, right?”
